  "adaptation": {
    "semantic": "\"day\" can mean twenty-four hours (*three days*) or only the hours of light (*day and night*). Many languages have separate words for these two meanings.",
    "grammar": "Days and dates take **on** (*on Friday*); **every day**, **the next day**, **one day**, and **the other day** take no preposition. **Every day** (adverb) and **everyday** (adjective) are different.",
    "culture": null,
